rows.jobDuty:
1. Develop monthly work plans for the department, lead and supervise employees to complete target tasks, monitor and inspect the implementation of various work systems, and coordinate with upstream and downstream departments;
2. After operations are completed, organise the inventory area, clean up packaging materials, adjust storage locations, organise product categories, and handle discrepancies;
3. Supervise the implementation of management systems, manage employee attendance, provide necessary job-related training to staff, and evaluate work performance;  
4. Plan product categories in storage areas to optimise physical space utilisation, maintain temporary storage zones, and conduct daily warehouse;  
5. Manage the receipt, issuance, and storage of warehouse goods;  
6. Implement and revise warehouse management systems, standardise operational procedures, optimise internal processes, and ensure their effective implementation;
7. Ensure inventory records are clear and accurate, conduct regular warehouse inventories, and verify the accuracy of inventory data in accordance with warehouse management regulations;
8. Oversee overall inventory management within the warehouse, coordinate and execute inventories (such as daily counts), ensure inventory records match physical stock, and investigate discrepancies in inventory items.

rows.jobRequirement:
1. Minimum 5 years' management experience within large-scale retail or warehousing/logistics enterprises, with warehouse operations experience advantageous;
2. Demonstrated expertise across multiple supply chain functions including inbound management, outbound management, inventory control, staff capability development, and warehouse standardisation;
3. Excellent communication skills, strong execution capabilities, and a well-developed strategic perspective;
4. Demonstrate enthusiasm for the role, with a proactive approach to problem-solving and process optimisation;
5. Possess comprehensive knowledge of warehouse logistics management, warehouse safety protocols, and operational procedures;
6. Proficiency in English, with the ability to thrive in a multilingual work environment.
